  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Services Projects Process About Blog Contact Overview Buy Rosewood Services Projects Process About Blog Contact [email protected] +00 00 00 00 00 Published November 4, 2025 How Rosewood builds reliable spaces A behind-the-scenes look at how our framing crews prepare every renovation for success, from load calculations to weather-ready materials. Every project we touch starts with a solid frame. That might sound obvious for a construction company, but framing is where long-term durability, precise finishes, and client trust are really forged. Here\u2019s how the Rosewood crew approaches every structural build-out. 1. Start with the load path Before a single stud goes up, our team reviews architectural drawings and onsite measurements to confirm the loads flowing from roof to foundation. We calculate bearing points, verify joist spans, and double-check engineered beams so the finished space feels solid underfoot. 2. Work with seasoned materials We source kiln-dried lumber and moisture-resistant sheathing to minimize twisting or shrinkage as the home acclimates. On larger additions, we\u2019ll often specify LVL or PSL beams to keep floor plans open without compromising strength.",
